   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "וְעַד כָּאן הָיִינוּ בָּאִין בַּשַּׁבָּת. קָסָבַר: תְּחוּמִין דְּרַבָּנַן.",
   "en": "«And» the mishna states that one is deemed credible to testify, in his adulthood, that he saw as a minor: «Until here we would come on Shabbat.» The Gemara explains: This tanna «maintains» that the Shabbat «boundaries,» beyond which one may not go outside the city on Shabbat, are mandated «by rabbinic» law, and the Sages deemed him credible in matters of rabbinic law."
